---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base
  title="Privacy | Cyber Pirate Labs"
  description="How the Cyber Pirate Labs website stores demo inquiries. Owner review required."
>
  <section class="page-intro legal-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Cyber Pirate Labs / Website information</p>
      <p class="flag"><strong>Owner review required.</strong> This page describes the inquiry system in this repository. Confirm it before treating it as the company’s privacy notice.</p>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p>Cyber Pirate Labs, LLC operates this website for CPL Command Center. The only personal information the site is built to collect is what you type into the inquiry form.</p>
      <h2>What the form stores</h2>
      <p>The form asks for your name, email, and what you want to automate. Company is optional. A sample-workflow label may be included when you follow a link from the preview. The walkthrough itself does not create an inquiry. There is no marketing list on this form.</p>
      <p>The site also stores a submission id, a reference id, the time, a hash of the network address, a shortened browser string, and the status of later delivery steps. It does not store the raw network address. There is no account, no payment, and no file upload.</p>
      <h2>Where it goes</h2>
      <p>A valid inquiry is saved in a private Cloudflare D1 database for this website. That save is what “saved” means. A later step can copy the inquiry into a private Google Sheet and Drive folder and notify a business inbox. Those steps are tracked separately. If they are not configured, or if they fail, the inquiry remains stored and a scheduled job retries delivery with a limited backoff. Success on the form is not a claim that every later step already finished.</p>
      <p>Google and notification delivery are not active until the owner adds those credentials. This deployment may therefore save an inquiry locally to the site database only.</p>
      <h2>Verification and abuse controls</h2>
      <p>Production uses Cloudflare Turnstile. There is no bypass that skips verification. The form also uses rate limits, a hidden field that should stay empty, and same-origin checks. Operators can review pending delivery, retry it, export a private CSV, confirm that a Google copy arrived, or delete a record. There is no public list of inquiries.</p>
      <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
      <p>No advertising pixels. No session replay. No sale of inquiry data. No certification is claimed for SOC 2, HIPAA, or GDPR. Deletion removes the inquiry row and keeps a short deletion note with the reference id and time, not the message.</p>
      <h2>How long it is kept</h2>
      <p>Until an authorized operator deletes it. This page does not invent a retention period.</p>
      <p>Questions about a stored inquiry can be sent through the same form. Include the reference id if you have one.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Contact Aaron <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
